[=DESCRIPTION]
Serves pre-fetched CrowdStrike Falcon inventory data over HTTP. Reads the JSONL
datasets and manifest produced by \fBfemur\fR from a data directory
(\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR) and exposes them via a local REST API. Optionally re-fetches
data in the background when it grows older than \fB\-\-max\-age\fR, using the
credentials in \fB\-\-env\-file\fR.
.PP
femurd runs on uvicorn. For development, \fB\-\-reload\fR enables auto-reload; for
production, \fB\-\-workers\fR sets the process count. See \fBFILES\fR and
\fBENVIRONMENT\fR below.
.PP

[>ENVIRONMENT]
.TP
.B CLIENT_ID, CLIENT_SECRET, BASE_URL
CrowdStrike API credentials and region used by background re-fetch jobs. Read from
the file given to \fB\-\-env\-file\fR (or the environment).
.TP
.B FALCON_INVENTORY_DATA_DIR, FALCON_INVENTORY_ENV_FILE, FALCON_INVENTORY_MAX_AGE
Set by femurd from the corresponding command-line options and read by the uvicorn
worker processes. Normally you do not set these by hand.

[>FILES]
.TP
.B <data-dir>/manifest.json
Manifest describing the datasets femurd serves; produced by \fBfemur\fR.
.TP
.B <data-dir>/
Directory of JSONL/XML dataset files produced by \fBfemur \-\-output\-dir\fR.
.TP
.B .env
Credentials file for background re-fetch (\fB\-\-env\-file\fR). Keep it mode 0600.

[>EXAMPLES]
.TP
Serve inventory on the default local address and port:
.B femurd \-\-data\-dir ./inventory
.TP
Serve with credentials for background re-fetch, on a custom port:
.B femurd \-d ./inventory \-e talon1.env \-\-port 9000
.TP
Bind all interfaces with multiple workers (behind a reverse proxy):
.B femurd \-d ./inventory \-\-host 0.0.0.0 \-\-workers 4

[>SUPPORT]
FEMUR (Falcon Exposure Management Universal Reporter) is a community-driven, open
source project, not a CrowdStrike product. As such, it carries no formal support,
expressed or implied. For issue reporting guidance, questions, and confidentiality
considerations, see the project on GitHub:
.PP
.B https://github.com/cs-shadowbq/falcon-exposure-management-universal-reporter
.PP
Report issues at:
.B https://github.com/cs-shadowbq/falcon-exposure-management-universal-reporter/issues

[>SEE ALSO]
.B femur (1)
produces the inventory datasets that femurd serves.
.PP
When installed as a systemd service, femurd runs sandboxed (see the shipped
femur-server.service unit and INSTALL.md). Verify with:
.B systemd-analyze security femur
